  "id": "DrugBank_DB00153 - MONDO_5298",
  "verbalization": "Ergocalciferol, also known as vitamin D3, is implicated in the pathogenesis of osteoporosis through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Ergocalciferol is linked to Osteoporosis via a chain of indications that ultimately involve Cholecalciferol, a form of vitamin D. Path_10171 indicates that Ergocalciferol is associated with Hypercalcemia, which is linked to Calcium Gluconate, and Calcium Gluconate is linked to Osteoporosis. Path_10168 and Path_10169 show that Ergocalciferol is associated with Obsolete Vitamin D Deficiency and Osteomalacia, both of which are linked to Cholecalciferol, which in turn is linked to Osteoporosis. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Ergocalciferol may contribute to the development of osteoporosis, though the exact role of each step remains to be clarified. The evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship that involves vitamin D metabolism and calcium homeostasis, but the integration of these pathways into a single, coherent mechanism requires further investigation.",
